        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0787c4a1-04cc-5a98-bcfa-a525e46b0266",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Zenon B. Lukosius, elder Moore\n- Military Units and Vessels: U.S. Navy, German submarine U-505, Kriegsmarine\n- Works: Playing with the Enemy\n- Events: World War II, capture of U-505, prisoner of war detention\n\nFacts:\n- Zenon B. Lukosius was born on August 24, 1918, and he was a Lithuanian–American World War II veteran.\n- In 1944, Zenon B. Lukosius was a member of the U.S. Navy crew that captured the German submarine U-505.\n- U-505 was a German Type IXC U-boat built for Nazi Germany's Kriegsmarine during World War II.\n- The book Playing with the Enemy takes its title from elder Moore's time as a guard in a top-secret prisoner of war camp that held the crew of the captured German submarine U-505.\n- Zenon B. Lukosius died on August 12, 2006.",
